Document.description_en:
The Proposed Project 

&nbsp;

Eabametoong First Nation is proposing the development of a subdivision on the east end of the community&#39;s core to address the community&#39;s ongoing housing crisis. The subdivision will include 266 subdivision lots and 50 rural lots with the project footprint totalling 125.7 ha. Development with be divided into the following 4 phases; Phase 1 - construction of 48 lots, Phase 2 &ndash; construction of 58 lots and 16 rural lots, Phase 3 &ndash; construction of 83 lots and 11 rural lots, and Phase 4 &ndash; construction of 45 lots and 23 rural lots. The scope of work of each phase will include:


	Tree clearing, grubbing and grading the lots;
	Construction of granular driveways and walkways;
	Construction of drainage ditches along the roadways;
	The construction of new roads to lots;
	Extension of the electrification network from the diesel generating station (DGS) to the new lot locations;
	Complete electrical service connections to the lot boundaries;
	Extension of the water distribution network by installing a trunk watermain along the Main Road to the east end development area and watermain along the new road for lots;
	Installation of water service connections to lots from the new water distribution system;
	Construct sanitary sewers, sewage pumping station and associated force main for lots;
	Install sanitary service connections to the lots from the new sanitary collection system.


Infrastructure required includes:


	Access roads in the subdivision, drainage ditching, culverts, telecommunication lines, overhead electrical lines, and water and sewer piping.


Activities involved throughout the project lifecycle includes:&nbsp;


	Tree clearing, land grading, bedrock blasting, road construction and utility installation.


Waste generation may include:


	Excess soil temporarily stockpiled and used for landscaping the residential lots, logs from tree clearing will be piled and made available to community members.


Quarry materials to be used:


	Borrow granular materials wil be utilized for road base construction.
	Borrow sand materials will be utilized for pipe bedding.


&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Document.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation d&#39;Eabametoong propose l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un lotissement &agrave; l&#39;est du centre-ville afin de rem&eacute;dier &agrave; la crise du logement qui s&eacute;vit dans la communaut&eacute;. Ce lotissement comprendra 266 lots et 50 lots ruraux, pour une superficie totale de 125,7 hectares. Le d&eacute;veloppement sera divis&eacute; en quatre phases : phase 1 &ndash; construction de 48 lots, phase 2 &ndash; construction de 58 lots et 16 lots ruraux, phase 3 &ndash; construction de 83 lots et 11 lots ruraux, et phase 4 &ndash; construction de 45 lots et 23 lots ruraux. Les travaux pr&eacute;vus pour chaque phase comprendront :


	D&eacute;boisement, dessouchage et nivellement des lots&nbsp;;
	Construction d&#39;all&eacute;es et de trottoirs en gravier&nbsp;;
	Cr&eacute;ation de foss&eacute;s de drainage le long des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s&nbsp;;
	Construction de nouvelles routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s aux terrains&nbsp;;
	Extension du r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique depuis la centrale diesel jusqu&#39;aux nouveaux lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements &eacute;lectriques complets aux limites des lots&nbsp;;
	Extension du r&eacute;seau de distribution d&#39;eau par l&#39;installation d&#39;une conduite principale le long de la route principale jusqu&#39;&agrave; la zone d&#39;am&eacute;nagement est et d&#39;une conduite le long de la nouvelle route desservant les lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements d&#39;eau potable aux lots &agrave; partir du nouveau r&eacute;seau de distribution&nbsp;;
	Construction des &eacute;gouts sanitaires, de la station de pompage des eaux us&eacute;es et de la conduite de refoulement associ&eacute;e pour les lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements d&#39;eau potable aux terrains &agrave; partir du nouveau r&eacute;seau d&#39;assainissement.


Les infrastructures requises comprennent&nbsp;:


	Voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s au lotissement, foss&eacute;s de drainage, ponceaux, lignes de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications, lignes &eacute;lectriques a&eacute;riennes et r&eacute;seaux d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts.


Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues tout au long du cycle de vie du projet comprennent&nbsp;:


	D&eacute;boisement, nivellement du terrain, dynamitage de la roche m&egrave;re, construction de routes et installation de services publics.


G&eacute;n&eacute;ration de d&eacute;chets&nbsp;:


	La terre exc&eacute;dentaire sera temporairement entrepos&eacute;e et utilis&eacute;e pour l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager des terrains r&eacute;sidentiels. Les billots provenant de la d&eacute;forestation seront empil&eacute;s et mis &agrave; la disposition des r&eacute;sidents.


Mat&eacute;riaux de carri&egrave;re utilis&eacute;s&nbsp;:


	Des mat&eacute;riaux granulaires emprunt&eacute;s seront utilis&eacute;s pour la construction de la fondation routi&egrave;re.
	Du sable d&#39;emprunt sera utilis&eacute; pour le lit de pose des canalisations.


&nbsp;

